{
  "schema_version": "value.known-data-objects/v1",
  "notes": [
    "Truth registry of released research data objects (plan 4.5 scheme 5). Keyed by the object's sha256; series_reader.registry_entry uses an entry only after the bytes on disk hash to its key (and to the binding's declared sha256).",
    "Field status: declared (the binding's own declaration is right), registry_asserted (the registry's value replaces or completes the binding), declared_unverified (the binding declares it, nobody verified it).",
    "repairs index the object's data rows under the asserted csv_header (0 = first data row). drop_source_rows removes duplicated source rows (the later publication is kept); interpolate_gaps inserts linearly interpolated periods, applied in order.",
    "defects are what a validation layer reports for the object (plan 4.5 S4); correction_ids are the universal corrections (decision A5) whose reading repair the entry carries. Evidence: VALUE review 2026-10-04 P6-02/P6-03/P6-04 and the R029 approved_r03 interconnector manifest and demand__utc_2022/audit.json.",
    "GBP1 public1 interconnector flow files are labelled MWh/period but hold instantaneous MW (review P6-12); the registry asserts MW so the structural unit check reads them as MW with a warning."
  ],
  "fx_bases": {
    "value.approved-eur-gbp-1.1/r029-approved-r03": {
      "eur_per_gbp": 1.1,
      "source": "VALUE-UK calendar pack R029 (value-uk-calendar-vx-trade001), files/interconnectors__approved_r03/manifest.json: 'Ember 2022 except Ireland 2021; approved fixed EUR/GBP 1.1'; source EUR/MWh divided by 1.1 once, each UTC hour expanded to two periods once.",
      "price_year": 2022
    }
  },
